            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="0868" n="754" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg754"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1340</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Latin
                        American Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-17">August 17, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Argentine Ambassador, Señor Felipe Espil, called to comply with instructions
                    received from the Foreign Office at Buenos Aires to inform the Department (as
                    well as the representatives of the other neutral states) that Argentina has
                    abandoned its representations to the Bolivian and Paraguayan Governments with
                    respect to an international police service, in view of the possible conflict of
                    those representations with the representations of the neutral governments.
                    Argentina is, however, continuing its efforts in behalf of the renewal of
                    diplomatic relations between Bolivia and Paraguay, although these efforts are
                    temporarily suspended pending the arrival at Buenos Aires of Señor Sanchez
                    Bustamante from La Paz.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter C.
                    Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
